  "reply": "`parseDuration` in `src/duration.ts` now follows the spec, and `bun test` passes (26 tests, 0 failures). That is the only file I changed.\n\n- **Format:** it takes one or more `<digits><unit>` components in strictly descending h, m, s, ms order. Whitespace is allowed before and after each component and at both ends.\n- **Rejections:** it throws `RangeError` for empty input, duplicate or out-of-order units, signs, fractions and junk. It also throws if the running total goes over `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`.\n- **Space before the unit:** the existing tests expect `\"1 s\"` to be rejected, so whitespace between a number and its unit is not allowed.\n- **Large values:** totals are summed as `BigInt`, so very large inputs are caught exactly, without rounding errors.\n- **Project rules:** the export is unchanged, there are no new dependencies, and I didn't edit the tests.",
